# Manga Generator

> With the shared Skill, read documentation in the installed engine/. Replace `node cli/NAME.mjs ARGS` with `node <skill>/scripts/run.mjs <workspace> NAME ARGS`, and set MANGA_PROJECT relative to the workspace. Do not copy code or documentation into the workspace. Standalone reproducibility packages retain their own executable CLI.

English | [日本語](README.md)

A manga production tool for working with Codex to turn a novel or other source text into a script, storyboards, generated artwork, lettering, reviewed pages, and a PDF.

Text and speech bubbles are placed separately from the artwork, making dialogue easier to revise later.

## Codex Agent Skill

Start with the distributed skill's `SKILL.md`. Invoke `$manga-generator` to adapt a complete source, revise a work, or resume production. Codex handles image generation and visual reviews; bundled CLI commands handle layout, history, and validation.

Run these commands from the **skill folder containing SKILL.md and scripts/**. Each destination must be a new directory.

```sh
node scripts/setup.mjs workspace /absolute/new-workspace
node scripts/setup.mjs bundle /absolute/new-skill-copy
```

Run production commands with the Skill’s scripts/run.mjs, passing the workspace and command. Runtime code stays in the Skill. That workspace does not contain the skill's setup helper; use the original skill folder for redistribution. Personal sources, images, and production history are excluded. Codex follows the skill's `references/environment.md` to prepare the environment.

